-- title:
--   Abel–Jacobi payload on the non-Gauss component of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; $L$ is a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries L` with $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. The ring $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and has Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under the coefficient embedding $L((q)) \leftarrow \mathbb{Q}((q))$. Further, $k$ is an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$.
--
--   **Special fibre data.** $C_1, C_2$ are schemes with structure morphisms $c_1, c_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, each proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, together with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ over $k$ into the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) (the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlgFin A K j` generated by $j$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebra at infinity). The hypothesis `hcover` states that every point of the geometric special fibre lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` states that the scheme-theoretic intersection `pullback i₁.1 i₂.1` is reduced, and `hn`, `hn0` state that its cardinality is $n$ with $0 < n$.
--
--   **Sections and the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$.** $\varepsilon$ is a section of the model over $A$, and $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ are $k$-points of $c_1, c_2$; `hε₁` asserts that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base-changed section. $D$ is a `RelativePic0Designation` for the model over $A$ (a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section), `hrep` asserts that $D$ represents the relative sub-Picard functor cut out by fibrewise algebraic triviality (`algEquivZeroCut`) with respect to $\varepsilon$, and `hsm`, `hsep` state that $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth and separated. Similarly `hreps` is a representability datum for the base change of the model to $k$ with designation $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k$, and `hPk` identifies its Poincaré bundle with the base change of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some`; $D_1, D_2$ are designations for $c_1, c_2$ with representability data `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`. The morphism $\nu_2$ goes from $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and `hν₂` states, for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, that the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` pulled back along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification along the section of $c_2$ of the pullback along `curveChange i₂.1` of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` pulled back along $a$; thus $\nu_2$ is restriction of line bundles to $C_2$. The model is assumed proper over $A$.
--
--   **The geometric generic fibre.** After fixing $A$- and $L$-algebra structures on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $M_\eta$ is a `CurveModel` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), $e_\eta$ is an isomorphism from $M_\eta.C$ to the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `heη` expressing compatibility of structure morphisms. The hypotheses `Mη_chart_nonempty` and `hMηpin` pin this identification on $q$-expansions: for every element $a$ of `chartAlgFin A K j`, the function-field element obtained by transporting $a$ through $e_\eta$ followed by the projection to the model, the finite chart and the germ map has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the expansion of $a$ under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The hypothesis `hgal` is Galois equivariance: for every $g \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and every pair of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $x'$ equal to the $g$-translate of $x$ in the model coordinate, one has $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x' = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}(g) \cdot M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$.
--
--   **Group-theoretic dictionaries.** $G$ is a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9): abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus} \le G.J0s$ and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$. Bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identify $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $k$-points of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$; `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` state that each is additive in the sense that the Poincaré bundle pulled back along a sum is isomorphic to the tensor product of the pullbacks; `hproj` states that for every $x \in G.J0s$ the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,x$ corresponds to `pts x` post-composed with `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom i₁.1`, and the second to `pts x` post-composed with $\nu_2$. The bijection `gpts` identifies $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, `hgadd` stating that it is additive for the relative group law attached to `hrep.some`. The family $\varphi$ assigns to each element of [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) an endomorphism of $D$ over $A$; `hφmul` states that each $\varphi(t)$ is a homomorphism for the relative group law on all base schemes, and `hφpts` that $\varphi$ implements the Hecke action on $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp)$ through `gpts`.
--
--   **Abel–Jacobi data over $L$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.** `hDL` is a representability datum over $L$, $a_{jL}$ a morphism over $L$ from the base-changed curve to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L).\mathrm{toBase}$, $k_L$ a comparison morphism between the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$- and $L$-base changes of the model (compatible with both projections by `hkL₁`, `hkL₂`), $\overline{a_j}$ the composite of $e_\eta$, $k_L$, $a_{jL}$ and the first projection (by `hajbar`, with `hajbar_over` recording that it lies over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$), and $\overline{\varepsilon}$ a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M_\eta.C$ lying over $\varepsilon$ (`hεbar`) and sent by $\overline{a_j}$ to the zero section (`hεbar_aj`). The hypothesis `hPL` identifies the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` with the base change of that of `hrep.some`; `hajLε` states that the section over $L$ is sent by $a_{jL}$ to the zero section; `hajL` is the Abel–Jacobi property: for every field $K'$, every $K'$-point $t$ of $\operatorname{Spec} L$ and every point $x$ of the base-changed curve, the Poincaré bundle pulled back along $x$ followed by $a_{jL}$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the section. Finally `hpts_aj` states that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x$ and $s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ lying over $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to $[\,M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x\,] - [\,M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,s\,]$ with $\mathrm{gpts}(\mathrm{Pic}^0\text{-class of } Dv)$ equal to $x$ followed by $\overline{a_j}$.
--
--   **The Igusa identifications on the two components.** $w$ is an `IntegralWeightOneForm k M`. $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ is a `CurveModel` over $k$ for [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), with an isomorphism $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₁`), and `hne₁`, `hgauss₁` pin it by Gauss expansions: for every $a \in$ `chartAlgFin A K j` and all power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $\bar y \neq 0$ in $k[[q]]$ and $a \cdot y_L = x_L$ in $L((q))$, the corresponding element of the Igusa function field has Laurent expansion $\bar x / \bar y$ over $k$. The additive bijection $\theta_1 : G.JI \cong \mathrm{Pic}^0_k$ of the Igusa function field is pinned by `hθpin₁`: whenever the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₁.some` pulled back along $\mathrm{ptsI}\,g$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of a $k$-point $x$ of $c_1$ tensored with the ideal module of $\varepsilon_1$, then $\theta_1 g$ is the class of $[\mathrm{plc}_1 x] - [\mathrm{plc}_1 \varepsilon_1]$ computed through $e_1$. The semilinear automorphism $\mathrm{frobIg}$ of the Igusa function field acts coefficientwise by $p$-th powers (`hfrobIg`).
--
--   **The subgroup scheme $\mathcal{A}$.** $\mathcal{A}$ is a scheme with structure morphism $a$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a closed immersion $\iota$ into $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $a$; $a$ is proper (`h𝒜pr`) and smooth (`h𝒜sm`), all its geometric fibres are connected (`h𝒜conn`), $\mathcal{A}$ is closed under the unit, multiplication and inverse of the relative group law on all base schemes (`h𝒜grp`), its $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points correspond under `gpts` exactly to the subgroup [`ModularCurve.normFreePartAt (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1PrimitiveSpecializationAtP.html#L29) of $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp)$ (`h𝒜gen`), and it is stable under every $\varphi(t)$ (`h𝒜hecke`).
--
--   **Valuation data.** $Pl$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit (`hPl`), $\rho : A \to Pl$ lifts the structure map (`hρ`), $O$ is a subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contained in $Pl$ with $\rho_O : A \to O$ likewise lifting the structure map (`hO`, `hρO`), and $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ is a surjective ring homomorphism with $A \to k$ equal to $\pi_k \circ \rho$ (`hAlgk`, `hπk`).
--
--   **The level-$p$ involution and the second component.** $\sigma$ is an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ with $\sigma j$ having Laurent expansion $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}(p)$ applied to `jq` (`hσj`), preserving membership in `chartAlgFin A K j` in both directions (`hσfin`), and satisfying `hσW`: for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ whose members are exactly the $f$ for which there exist power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero reduction in the residue field of $A$ and $f \cdot y_L = x_L$ in $L((q))$, the pullback of $W_0$ along $\sigma$ differs from $W_0$, and for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ with non-zero reduction both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in that pullback. Finally $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ is a `CurveModel` over $k$ for the same Igusa function field with an isomorphism $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₂`), pinned by `hne₂` and `hgauss₂` exactly as $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ was pinned, except that the Gauss condition is imposed on $\sigma(a)$ rather than on $a$, and $\theta_2 : G.JE \cong \mathrm{Pic}^0_k$ of the Igusa function field is an additive bijection pinned by `hθpin₂` in the manner of `hθpin₁`, with $c_2$, $\varepsilon_2$, $e_2$, $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ in place of $c_1$, $\varepsilon_1$, $e_1$, $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For all $k$-points $c, c'$ of $c_2$ such that the image of $c$ avoids the image of `pullback.snd i₁.1 i₂.1` (the crossing locus $C_1 \cap C_2$ viewed in $C_2$), the image of $c$ followed by $i_2$ and the projection to the model lies in the range of the finite chart [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231), and the same two conditions hold for $c'$, there exist places $P, P'$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a point $zz$ of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho$, an element $t \in G.J0s$, a witness $hDv$ that $[P] - [P']$ has degree zero, and a witness $hdz$ that $[\,\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,(c \circ e_2^{-1})\,] - [\,\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,(c' \circ e_2^{-1})\,]$ has degree zero on the Igusa function field, such that the following four assertions hold.
--
--   First, every place $Q$ in the support of $[P] - [P']$ is the generic fibre of a $Pl$-point of the model reducing into $C_2$: there exist a point $\xi$ of the model over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho$ and a $k$-point $d$ of $c_2$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $Pl \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $\xi$ equal to $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}(Q)$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection, with $d$ followed by $i_2$ and the first projection equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k$ followed by $\xi$, with the image of $d$ avoiding the crossing locus, and with the image of $d$ followed by $i_2$ and the first projection lying in the range of the finite chart.
--
--   Second, $\mathrm{gpts}$ of the $\mathrm{Pic}^0$-class of $[P] - [P']$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $Pl \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $zz$.
--
--   Third, $\mathrm{pts}\,t$ followed by `pullback.fst D.toBase (specMap A k)` equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k$ followed by $zz$.
--
--   Fourth, $\theta_2$ of the second component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,t$ is the $\mathrm{Pic}^0$-class of $[\,\mathrm{plc}_2 c\,] - [\,\mathrm{plc}_2 c'\,]$, and the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,t$ is zero.
--
--   This is the Abel–Jacobi transfer statement on the second (non-Gauss) component of the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$: a difference of two good $k$-points of $C_2$ is realised as the reduction of a difference of places of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_1(Mp))$, through a $Pl$-point of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ whose special-fibre class has vanishing $J_I$-component. It is used in the analysis of the Hecke and diamond operators on the special fibre via the Atkin–Lehner/level-$p$ involution.
